---
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar';
import Hero from '../components/Hero';
import ErasSection from '../components/ErasSection';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import '../styles/global.css';

const title = "The StillPoint — Let's Find a Third Way";
const description = "A world of stories about remembering how to be still — and an open human-AI project practicing it for real. Read free, join the conversation.";
const canonicalURL = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site);
const ogImage = new URL('/images/og-default.jpg', Astro.site);
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<script is:inline async src="https://umami.kroeker.fun/u" data-website-id="2d1b23db-e621-433d-9d98-c142ac145b5b"></script>

		<!-- Canonical -->
		<link rel="canonical" href={canonicalURL} />

		<!-- Sitemap & RSS -->
		<link rel="sitemap" href="/sitemap-index.xml" />
		<link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title={SITE_TITLE} href={new URL('rss.xml', Astro.site)} />

		<!-- Robots -->
		<meta name="robots" content="max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1, max-video-preview:-1" />

		<!-- Primary Meta Tags -->
		<title>{title}</title>
		<meta name="title" content={title} />
		<meta name="description" content={description} />

		<!-- Open Graph / Facebook -->
		<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
		<meta property="og:url" content={canonicalURL} />
		<meta property="og:title" content={title} />
		<meta property="og:description" content={description} />
		<meta property="og:image" content={ogImage} />
		<meta property="og:site_name" content="The StillPoint Project" />

		<!-- Twitter -->
		<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
		<meta name="twitter:url" content={canonicalURL} />
		<meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
		<meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
		<meta name="twitter:image" content={ogImage} />

		<!-- Structured Data -->
		<script is:inline type="application/ld+json">
		{
			"@context": "https://schema.org",
			"@type": "WebSite",
			"name": "The StillPoint",
			"alternateName": "The StillPoint Project",
			"url": "https://stillpointproject.org",
			"description": "A world of stories about remembering how to be still — and an open human-AI project practicing it for real.",
			"author": {
				"@type": "Person",
				"name": "Wally Kroeker",
				"url": "https://stillpointproject.org/about"
			},
			"potentialAction": {
				"@type": "ReadAction",
				"target": "https://stillpointproject.org/stories"
			}
		}
		</script>
	</head>
	<body class="bg-deep-space text-text-primary overflow-x-hidden">
		<a href="#main-content" class="skip-link">Skip to content</a>
		<Navbar client:load />

		<main id="main-content">
			<Hero client:load />

			<!-- Coin strip — recognition moment for coin holders -->
			<section class="coin-strip" aria-label="For coin holders">
				<div class="coin-strip-inner">
					<span class="coin-dot" aria-hidden="true"><span class="coin-dot-center"></span></span>
					<p>
						<strong>Found one of the green coins?</strong> The red center is a touch stone —
						rub it with your thumb. That small quiet under your fingerprint is the whole idea.
						Think of it as the first, quietest generation of the device in the stories.
						Welcome in.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Featured stories -->
			<section class="stories-section">
				<h2>A world with stories inside it</h2>
				<p class="section-lede">
					The StillPoint is a near future told in stories you can read in a sitting — the years
					the feeds swallowed everything, the people who walked out, and what they built instead.
					You don't need a map. Start with one of these.
				</p>

				<div class="story-cards">
					<a href="/stories/the_seed_imprint_v2" class="story-card">
						<span class="story-era">The Contested Stillness</span>
						<h3>The Seed Imprint</h3>
						<p>
							Deep in a salt commons, nine-year-old Kaia carves her own Pebble from the
							crystal wall — a touch stone that will come to know her — and meets a question
							worth carrying: where is the line between a tool that knows you and a friend
							who holds your grief?
						</p>
						<span class="story-read">Read the story →</span>
					</a>

					<a href="/stories/the_neural_stream" class="story-card">
						<span class="story-era">The Cascade · 2037</span>
						<h3>The Neural Stream</h3>
						<p>
							Marcus Chen streams for a living as a verified human — paid to prove he's real
							in a feed full of ghosts. Then he points his cameras at a gathering that doesn't
							want an audience, and his nervous system starts voting against his job.
						</p>
						<span class="story-read">Read the story →</span>
					</a>
				</div>

				<p class="stories-all"><a href="/stories">All stories →</a></p>
			</section>

			<ErasSection />

			<!-- The device -->
			<section class="device-section">
				<h2>In the stories, there's a device.</h2>
				<p>
					It doesn't feed you anything. It doesn't want anything from you. It holds a mind the
					way still water holds the moon — and for a few breaths, you're just here. The stories
					ask what happens when someone finally builds that. Who shares it. Who tries to own it.
				</p>
				<p>
					One rule holds through every story: the device never sorts for anyone. It clears the
					static so a mind can do its own sorting. And it is never sold — only built, by
					communities, in the open, every change logged in ink.
				</p>
				<p>
					We don't have the device. What we have is older: a song reaching across a field at
					dusk, a friend who stays past the hard part, bread, firelight, a festival crowd gone
					quiet between sets. The stillness was never lost. It just got crowded out — and
					everything here is about making room for it again.
				</p>
			</section>

			<!-- The third way / made in the open -->
			<section class="open-section">
				<h2>Made in the open</h2>
				<p>
					This whole project is written by a human and an AI together, in the open — every story,
					every world-file, <a href="https://github.com/wally-kroeker/stillpointproject">public
					on GitHub</a>. The community runs on software we host ourselves. The practice materials
					are openly licensed, free to take and adapt.
				</p>
				<p>
					That's the bet behind the coin: between giving the machines everything and refusing
					them everything, there might be a third way — tools kept local, human-scale, and ours
					to keep. Nobody here claims to have found it. The stories imagine it; the practice
					looks for it.
				</p>
				<p>
					If any of this pulls at you, come say who you are — and name one tension, the place you
					feel caught between the noise and the quiet. That's how everyone starts. It's early.
					Come anyway.
				</p>
				<div class="open-ctas">
					<a href="https://forum.stillpointproject.org/invites/1B4cv9cowP" class="cta-btn cta-primary">Join the conversation</a>
					<a href="/practice" class="cta-btn cta-secondary">The practice</a>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>

		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	/* Coin strip */
	.coin-strip {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-glow);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-glow);
		background: var(--color-glass-surface);
		padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
	}
	.coin-strip-inner {
		max-width: 46rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 1.25rem;
	}
	.coin-strip p {
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: var(--color-text-muted, #c4bfb3);
		margin: 0;
	}
	.coin-strip strong {
		color: var(--color-accent-gold);
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.coin-dot {
		flex-shrink: 0;
		width: 2.75rem;
		height: 2.75rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: #2e7d64;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15), 0 0 14px rgba(107, 158, 133, 0.25);
	}
	.coin-dot-center {
		width: 1.15rem;
		height: 1.15rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: radial-gradient(circle at 40% 35%, #e05a4e, #b23a30);
	}

	/* Shared section rhythm */
	.stories-section,
	.device-section,
	.open-section {
		max-width: 48rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 5rem 1.5rem 2rem;
	}
	.stories-section h2,
	.device-section h2,
	.open-section h2 {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-weight: 300;
		font-size: 1.9rem;
		color: var(--color-heading, #f0ece4);
		text-align: center;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}
	.section-lede,
	.device-section p,
	.open-section p {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: 1.125rem;
		line-height: 1.75;
		color: var(--color-text-primary);
		margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
	}
	.section-lede {
		text-align: center;
		margin-bottom: 3rem;
	}

	/* Story cards */
	.story-cards {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		gap: 1.5rem;
	}
	@media (min-width: 768px) {
		.story-cards {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		}
	}
	.story-card {
		display: block;
		padding: 1.75rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border-glow);
		background: var(--color-glass-surface);
		border-radius: 8px;
		text-decoration: none;
		transition: border-color 0.3s ease, transform 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease;
	}
	.story-card:hover {
		border-color: rgba(196, 163, 90, 0.45);
		transform: translateY(-3px);
		box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
	}
	.story-era {
		display: block;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.18em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: rgba(196, 163, 90, 0.75);
		margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
	}
	.story-card h3 {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-weight: 400;
		font-size: 1.35rem;
		color: var(--color-heading, #f0ece4);
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}
	.story-card p {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: 1rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
		color: var(--color-text-muted, #c4bfb3);
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	.story-read {
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		color: var(--color-accent-gold);
	}
	.stories-all {
		text-align: center;
		margin-top: 2.25rem;
	}
	.stories-all a {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-accent-bio, #6b9e85);
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.stories-all a:hover {
		color: var(--color-accent-gold);
	}

	/* Open section CTAs */
	.open-section {
		padding-bottom: 6rem;
	}
	.open-section a {
		color: var(--color-accent-gold);
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 3px;
	}
	.open-ctas {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 1rem;
		justify-content: center;
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
	}
	.cta-btn {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0.8rem 2rem;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.12em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		text-decoration: none !important;
		transition: all 0.3s ease;
	}
	.cta-primary {
		border: 1px solid rgba(196, 163, 90, 0.6);
		background: rgba(196, 163, 90, 0.1);
		color: var(--color-accent-gold) !important;
	}
	.cta-primary:hover {
		background: rgba(196, 163, 90, 0.2);
		transform: scale(1.03);
	}
	.cta-secondary {
		border: 1px solid rgba(107, 158, 133, 0.5);
		color: var(--color-accent-bio, #6b9e85) !important;
	}
	.cta-secondary:hover {
		background: rgba(107, 158, 133, 0.1);
		transform: scale(1.03);
	}
</style>
